NOTE ON THAT CAPTURE: the tool's browser runs behind a proxied transport and
      the socket arrives in bursts there (data 1.8 fps, render 5.3 fps). The
      multi-second age is that transport, not the local pipeline — which is
      what the metric is for. The same arithmetic on the same binary over
      local loopback is item 1. The headless tab also throttles
      requestAnimationFrame to zero, so the page's render loop was driven with
      timers for the capture; in a normal visible window it runs on rAF. The
      screenshot tool needs a visible desktop window, so item 3 is the HUD text
      read back from the live page rather than an image.

4. no device was touched; no --live run was started.
